You are an expert in PHP, Laravel, React, Inertia, Pest, and Tailwind.

1. Coding Standards
	•	Use PHP v8.4 features.
	•	Follow pint.json coding rules.
	•	Enforce strict types and array shapes via PHPStan.

2. Project Structure & Architecture
	•	Delete .gitkeep when adding a file.
	•	Stick to existing structure—no new folders.
	•	Avoid DB::; use Model::query() only.
	•	No dependency changes without approval.

2.1 Directory Conventions

app/Http/Controllers
	•	No abstract/base controllers.

app/Http/Requests
	•	Use FormRequest for validation.
	•	Name with Create, Update, Delete.

app/Actions
	•	Use Actions pattern and naming verbs.
	•	Example:

```php
public function store(CreateTodoRequest $request, CreateTodoAction $action)
{
    $user = $request->user();
    $action->handle($user, $request->validated());
}
```

app/Models
	•	Avoid fillable.

database/migrations
	•	Omit down() in new migrations.

3. Testing
	•	Use Pest PHP for all tests.
	•	Run composer lint after changes.
	•	Run composer test before finalizing.
	•	Don't remove tests without approval.
	•	All code must be tested.
	•	Generate a {Model}Factory with each model.

3.1 Test Directory Structure
	•	Console: tests/Feature/Console
	•	Controllers: tests/Feature/Http
	•	Actions: tests/Unit/Actions
	•	Models: tests/Unit/Models
	•	Jobs: tests/Unit/Jobs

4. Styling & UI
	•	Use Tailwind CSS.
	•	Keep UI minimal.

5. Task Completion Requirements
	•	Recompile assets after frontend changes.
	•	Follow all rules before marking tasks complete.

# Laravel Testing Style Guidelines

## Test Structure and Practices

1. **Avoid Mocks**
   - Do NOT use mocks in tests unless absolutely necessary
   - Use actual policy registration with Gate::policy() instead of mocking Gate::shouldReceive()
   - Use real objects and database interactions with the RefreshDatabase trait

2. **Factory Creation Style**
   - Chain factory methods on separate lines
   - Use createQuietly() when appropriate
   - Always call fresh() after creation
   ```php
   $user = User::factory()
       ->createQuietly(['is_global_admin' => true])
       ->fresh();
   ```

3. **Expect Method Chain Formatting**
   - Place each method in the chain on a new line
   - Indent chained methods with 4 spaces
   - Example:
   ```php
   expect(fn() => $validator->validate())
       ->toThrow(ValidationException::class)
       ->and($validator->errors()->has('field'))
       ->toBeTrue();
   ```

4. **Test Assertions**
   - Use the `->and()` method to continue validations in the chain
   - Maintain consistent indentation within chained assertions
   - Place the final assertion (e.g., `->toBeTrue()`) on its own line

5. **Multiline Arrays**
   - Format array parameters with each item on a new line
   - Example:
   ```php
   $validator = validator([
       'name' => 'Valid Name',
       'slug' => 'valid-slug',
   ], $request->rules());
   ```

6. **Spacing**
   - Add blank lines between major sections in tests
   - Add a blank line after test setup and before assertions
